#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplo en simulador a pequeña escala {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial implements a [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) to "
"simulate a one-dimensional (1D) Many-Body Localization (MBL) circuit. The "
"MBL circuit is a hardware-efficient circuit and is parameterized by two "
"parameters $\\theta$ and $\\vec{\\phi}$. When $\\theta$ is set to $0$ and "
"the initial state is prepared in $|0\\rangle$ for all the qubits, the ideal "
"expectation value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ is $+1$ for every qubit site "
"$i$ irrespective of the values of $\\vec{\\phi}$. More details on this "
"circuit are available in this "
"[article](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-57623-x).\n"
msgstr ""
"Este tutorial implementa un [patrón de Qiskit](/guides/intro-to-patterns) "
"para simular un circuito de Localización de Muchos Cuerpos (MBL) "
"unidimensional (1D). El circuito MBL es un circuito eficiente en hardware y "
"está parametrizado por dos parámetros $\\theta$ y $\\vec{\\phi}$. Cuando "
"$\\theta$ se establece en $0$ y el estado inicial se prepara en $|0\\rangle$"
" para todos los qubits, el valor esperado ideal de $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ "
"es $+1$ para cada sitio de qubit $i$, independientemente de los valores de "
"$\\vec{\\phi}$. Puedes consultar más detalles sobre este circuito en este "
"[artículo](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-57623-x).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that in a noiseless simulator, the expectation value obtained with and "
"without circuit cutting will be same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ten en cuenta que en un simulador sin ruido, el valor esperado obtenido con "
"y sin corte de circuito será el mismo.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 1: Transformar las entradas clásicas en un problema cuántico "
"{#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Construct the 1D MBL circuit {#construct-the-1d-mbl-circuit}"
msgstr "Construir el circuito MBL 1D {#construct-the-1d-mbl-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First, we present a function for constructing the 1D MBL circuit.\n"
msgstr "Primero presentamos una función para construir el circuito MBL 1D.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/a3debf65-06df-4277-933e-14b6f6170756-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/a3debf65-06df-4277-933e-14b6f6170756-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We calculate the average expectation value $O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_i Z_i$ "
"over all qubits for $\\theta = 0$. Since the ideal expectation value of "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle = 1$ $\\forall$ $i$, the ideal expectation value of "
"$O$ is also $1$. The parameters $\\phi$ are selected randomly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Calculamos el valor esperado promedio $O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_i Z_i$ sobre "
"todos los qubits para $\\theta = 0$. Dado que el valor esperado ideal de "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle = 1$ $\\forall$ $i$, el valor esperado ideal de $O$ "
"también es $1$. Los parámetros $\\phi$ se seleccionan aleatoriamente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit needs to be annotated by inserting **CutWire** in the desired "
"locations to partition it. For this tutorial, we opt for equal partition. "
"The MBL circuit is designed so that setting `use_cut=True` in the function "
"inserts the annotation properly after $\\frac{n}{2}$ qubits, $n$ being the "
"number of qubits in the original circuit. We also assigned the randomly "
"generated parameters to the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"El circuito debe anotarse insertando instrucciones **CutWire** en las "
"ubicaciones deseadas para particionarlo. Para este tutorial, optamos por una"
" partición equitativa. El circuito MBL está diseñado de modo que al "
"establecer `use_cut=True` en la función, la anotación se inserta "
"correctamente después de $\\frac{n}{2}$ qubits, siendo $n$ el número de "
"qubits en el circuito original. También asignamos los parámetros generados "
"aleatoriamente al circuito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/5208e0a8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/5208e0a8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 2: Optimizar el problema para la ejecución en hardware cuántico "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cut the circuit into smaller subcircuits {#cut-the-circuit-into-smaller-"
"subcircuits}"
msgstr ""
"Cortar el circuito en subcircuitos más pequeños {#cut-the-circuit-into-"
"smaller-subcircuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we partition the circuit into two smaller subcircuits using [`qiskit-"
"addon-cutting`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/). `qiskit-"
"addon-cutting` appends a virtual `Move` gate to split the wire cut location "
"by appropriately adjusting the number of qubits. Now we create the circuit "
"with this virtual gate. Since there is one wire cut, the number of "
"associated qubits will be increased by 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora particionamos el circuito en dos subcircuitos más pequeños usando "
"[`qiskit-addon-cutting`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/). "
"`qiskit-addon-cutting` agrega una compuerta virtual `Move` para dividir la "
"ubicación del corte de cable ajustando apropiadamente el número de qubits. "
"Ahora creamos el circuito con esta compuerta virtual. Dado que hay un corte "
"de cable, el número de qubits asociados aumentará en 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1834cb22-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1834cb22-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Construct and expand the observable {#construct-and-expand-the-observable}"
msgstr ""
"Construir y expandir el observable {#construct-and-expand-the-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The observable, as defined before, will be the average of $Z$ on each qubit."
" However, upon inserting the virtual `Move` gate, the effective number of "
"qubits in the circuit increases. The observable must also be expanded "
"accordingly to account for this change in the number of qubits. Note the "
"observable always acts trivially (as in $I$) on the extra qubit added for "
"the virtual `Move` gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"El observable, tal como se definió anteriormente, será el promedio de $Z$ en"
" cada qubit. Sin embargo, al insertar la compuerta virtual `Move`, el número"
" efectivo de qubits en el circuito aumenta. El observable también debe "
"expandirse en consecuencia para tener en cuenta este cambio en el número de "
"qubits. Observa que el observable siempre actúa de forma trivial (como $I$) "
"sobre el qubit adicional añadido para la compuerta virtual `Move`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now the circuit can be partitioned along the `Move` gate and we obtain the "
"subcircuits, as well as the subobservable, which is the portion of the "
"original observable associated with each subcircuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora el circuito puede particionarse a lo largo de la compuerta `Move` y "
"obtenemos los subcircuitos, así como el subobservable, que es la porción del"
" observable original asociada a cada subcircuito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here we visualize the two subcircuits:\n"
msgstr "Aquí visualizamos los dos subcircuitos:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1b0e779f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1b0e779f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/3c802f28-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/3c802f28-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Expanding the observable using the `Move` operation requires a `PauliList` "
"data structure. To reconstruct the expectation value of the original "
"circuit, we require the observable in the `SparsePauliOp` format.\n"
msgstr ""
"Expandir el observable usando la operación `Move` requiere una estructura de"
" datos `PauliList`. Para reconstruir el valor esperado del circuito "
"original, necesitamos el observable en formato `SparsePauliOp`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As discussed before, for each cut the upstream circuit must be measured in a"
" Pauli basis, and the downstream circuit must be prepared in the eigenstate "
"of the basis. The function `generate_cutting_experiments` creates all of "
"these necessary circuits and the coefficients associated with each circuit "
"required for reconstruction. Find more detail in [this "
"paper](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.150504).\n"
msgstr ""
"Como se explicó anteriormente, para cada corte el circuito aguas arriba debe"
" medirse en una base de Pauli, y el circuito aguas abajo debe prepararse en "
"el autoestado de esa base. La función `generate_cutting_experiments` crea "
"todos estos circuitos necesarios y los coeficientes asociados a cada "
"circuito requeridos para la reconstrucción. Consulta más detalles en [este "
"artículo](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.150504).\n"

